{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031447-mysterium-priorieties","id":1031447,"title":"Mysterium Priorieties","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-13T21:52:06-08:00","id":1031447,"title":"Mysterium Priorieties","content":"I'm prepering to run Mysterium Caucus scene in Boston setting. The problem is - What it should really be about? Should Mystygouges discuss their progress on big Mysferies of tbe region? ( Like Spirit of the Land or Secret Concord? ) Or maybe they should talk about latest findings for the Atheneum? Or some members should read their 'papers' that will become proper Grimoires? Or they should sit in circle and chant to Egregore?<br /> <br /> Basicly, my question is simple - What Mysterium DO on their meetings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T22:44:24-08:00","id":1031462,"title":"","content":"I tend to see the Mysterium as a group of magical academics, so I would see them starting with a highly ritualized ceremony claimed to be descended from Alexandria or some such, then dividing up into smaller groups for symposiums, presentations on new discoveries and meeting of equals debates on numerous subjects.<br /> \u200bI also picture a great deal of corduroy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T07:42:17-08:00","id":1031577,"title":"","content":"There is no Platonic Ideal of the Mysterium, ironically enough, at least manifested in the Fallen World. No two Caucuses will be identical.<br /> <br /> In one of the games I run, the Mysterium has three Caucuses in Oregon, with the one the player belongs to centering in the Northwest. The big local Mystery is the interstices and the strange flora and fauna that live within it. Since the Mages of the Caucus run politically primarily down lines that see cryptids in much the same way Teddy Roosevelt saw the wildlife of the United States (that is, it's beautiful, awe-inspiring, in need of protection and management, but it's also a resource for exploitation and an object of study), the Caucus's meeting place is full of such things.<br /> <br /> The meeting takes place in an enormous hall at a rounded table, surrounded by stuffed and mounted cryptids. The local Hierophant, Orcus, invokes the Mysteries in an opening prayer, greetings are exchanged, short matters of recognition are gotten out the way (i.e. if anyone has done anything of note in the last month, they get mentioned; thanks are given to those who supported the Caucus in an important manner recently; the host of the evening's events, which is always the local Curator, is thanked, etc.), and then everyone sits down to a meal.<br /> <br /> The meal is a part of the evening's events. It is made from the local cryptid flora and/or fauna, depending on what was available. In this way, it kind of resembles the Gastronomic Club of which Charles Darwin was a member. If a Mage was the one who brought in the ingredients, they inevitably get thanked at the start of the meeting. Recently, Mr. Hunt (and, yes, that is his Shadow Name), an ally of the player mystagogue, was credited for providing young sauropod flank steaks. Unfossilized dinosaur bones stand in the Athenaeum's collection thanks to him.<br /> <br /> After the meal, mystagogues are invited, in turn, to discuss the latest progress they've made and their expected contributions to the local Athenaeum(s) within the previous and coming month. Every Mage must make at least <i>one</i> contribution a month to maintain good standing and, while the threshold for that isn't very high (submitting a copy of your research notes is often enough), consistent low-effort contributions can see a member earning the ire of the Curators. Usually these presentations only last about ten to fifteen minutes but, when you have as many Mages as the Caucus does, that can be quite an ordeal just the same. The Curator and Hierophant are the only people in the room who can ask someone to cut it short, and they're loathe to do so because it's bad form to turn away knowledge.<br /> <br /> Once that's done with, the floor is opened to pressing business anyone might have. This lasts as long as it needs to, but this is rare. It's only really meant for discussing potential threats or interests for the entire Caucus. Occasionally, some Mage will bring up a breach of protocol by some other Mage or their cabal, and there will be discussion. If the Curator or Hierophant decide that there is sufficient cause for a decision, they will call a vote on the matter and all Mages present may vote on the matter. However, no Mage whose initiation is less than the greater of the accused or the plaintiff actually have any real say in the matter. Usually, it comes down to the Hierophant making a decision. Orcus is the oldest Mage left in the state in both years of life and Awakened experience, so his air of venerability means most matters he settles stay settled. People may disagree with his ruling, but he's widely considered a kind of sacred pillar of the Order; defy Orcus and... Well, how can you call yourself a mystagogue?<br /> <br /> After all this, Orcus adjourns the meeting and the Awakened are free to mingle. Most often, this means gravitating to someone whose work they found interesting and discussing it; sometimes prodding for a partnership on some matter. The Curator is usually the last to leave, or close to it. There's often some poor neokoros who gets left behind to clear the dishes, turn out the lights, and lock up. The duty is considered an honour, but it's basically a position fobbed off on the apprentice of the Curator or someone who wishes to get close to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> That became way longer than I intended it to, but my point is that no two Mysterium Caucuses are alike. Each is different. There will pretty much always be a sharing of knowledge and discussion at their meetings but beyond that, it really depends on who is in charge, the local beliefs of the Caucus, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T13:14:15-08:00","id":1032294,"title":"","content":"My ST has, so far, run the Mysterium caucus with no caucus wide meetings. We're in London, and in our setting there are more than a thousand mages in london. It's considered the magic capital of the world, partly because the true Giza pyramid stands there as a trophy won in a battle against the seers. It's a massive structure, and it's the athanaum of the city. Given how many mages there are and how international the city is, coordinating a caucus wide meeting simply isn't feasible.<br /> <br /> I guess, though, that really doesn't answer your question. I'd say the model that Axelgear has makes a lot of sense. You'd have to modify it for your caucus and the local big mystery. Whiiiiich in Boston would mean a much more hush-hush meeting given the nature of the local mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 01-15-2017, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T03:40:25-08:00","id":1032573,"title":"","content":"I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031562-typical-caucus-events\">'typical' Caucus compilation in this topic</a>. It has most typical things, those I can easily see in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> proposition, maybe just in unconventional order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T06:16:24-08:00","id":1032614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031447-mysterium-priorieties?p=1032294#post1032294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's considered the magic capital of the world, partly because the true Giza pyramid stands there as a trophy won in a battle against the seers. It's a massive structure, and it's the athanaum of the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do they keep it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T14:52:30-08:00","id":1032930,"title":"","content":"You'll have to walk the right path of High Runes to find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T06:47:06-08:00","id":1033984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031447-mysterium-priorieties?p=1032614#post1032614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where do they keep it?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a magically enlarged, co-located museum with anti-muggle wards. They've got a pair of identical twins that are part of the guard to the front door. You go down a large set of stairs in the museum past the guard at the desk. Naturally the stairs are warded so that people ignore them. When you get to the bottom, there's a door that acts as a portal to the other portion. Walk through and you are back at the foyar of the museum near the guard's desk, &quot;same&quot; guard there. However, the stairs this time are paved in gold, and the double doors at the bottom open up to a large room with a dome on top. There are several rooms leading off from there, one notably to the massive chamber that holds the athanaum. Interestingly, when you get to the pyramid you have to climb it to enter at the top. Restricted access is then enforced more tightly the further you go down inside the pyramid. <br /> <br /> For time's sake I am naturally not describing the structure in more detail. Suffice it to say there's a lot of gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:44:49-08:00","id":1034035,"title":"","content":"I am trying to contain my sides at the thought of wizards stealing the Pyramid of Giza. Oh my. Delightful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}